<chapter>

<title><classname>HttpdMemoryDataSource</classname> Reference</title>
 <section id="HttpdMemoryDataSource" xrefLabel="HttpdMemoryDataSource">
  <title>Introduction</title>
  <para>
  The <classname>HttpdMemoryDataSource</classname> is a class that 
  abstracts an addressable region of memory as a data source
  (see <xref linkend="HttpdDataSource">).
  </para>

  <note>
   <para>
    Only the methods in addition to those that are part of the abstract
    interface are documented here.
   </para>
  </note>

 </section>

 <section><title>Public Methods</title>

  <section><title><function>HttpdMemoryDataSource</function></title>
   <para>
    <funcsynopsis>
     <funcprototype>
      <funcdef>
       <function><classname>HttpdMemoryDataSource</classname>::HttpdMemoryDataSource</function>
      </funcdef>
      <paramdef>void *<parameter>p_data</parameter></paramdef>
      <paramdef>size_t <parameter>sz</parameter></paramdef>
     </funcprototype>
    </funcsynopsis>
   </para>

   <para>
   This function initializes a memory data source that points to 
   <parameter>p_data</parameter> and is <parameter>sz</parameter> bytes
   in length.
   </para>

  </section>
   
 </section>

</chapter>

